      "material": true,
      "rationale": "The local bytes and prompt/test contracts are directly validated, while hosted agent behavior, convergence quality, commit-bound CI, draft creation, release, installation, and activation remain separate unobserved gates.",
      "statement": "On this Windows host, the local v0.8.3 release-candidate tree passed 230 of 231 repository tests with one privilege-dependent symlink skip, both official validators, package and engine verification, offline replay-safe quality-loop conformance with no outbound action, and a non-mutating GitHub skill publication dry-run. The direct analyzer and reusable managed-skill maintainer prompts each authorize one isolated candidate attempt with at most three repair-and-recheck cycles and explicit clean-scope, repetition, unchanged-candidate, oscillation, forbidden-scope, missing-evidence, owner-decision, and cycle-limit stops. Skill invocation, quality receipts, issues, workflows, map acceptance, merge, release, publication, and installed update remain non-recursive and separately gated.",
      "status": "partially_supported"
    }
  ],
